# Rust
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# trycmd dump dirs (created when TRYCMD=dump)
**/dump/

# cargo-fuzz working dirs. Seed / regression corpora that we deliberately
# commit are added with `git add -f` per docs/fuzzing.md; the bulk
# Auto-generated corpus and crash artifacts stay out of git. Curated
# seed files (named, non-hash entries) are deliberately force-added
# with `git add -f` per docs/fuzzing.md rule 4.
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/coverage/

# .NET build output (adapters/Trace.Wpf, etc.). Scoped to adapters/ —
# a bare '**/bin/' also swallows Rust's src/bin/ convention directory
# and silently untracked an experiment binary's source (PR #20, D-010).
# examples/ holds .NET projects too, so it gets the same rule (Codex
# round-17 P2, D-043) — the D-010 scoping had silently unignored
# examples/DeclarationApp.Demo build output.
adapters/**/bin/
examples/**/bin/
**/obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local secrets and scratch
.env
.env.local
/scratch/
/notes-local/

# Trace artefacts (corpora and captured sessions stay out of git;
# only fixtures under `tests/fixtures/` are committed; see ADR-0007)
/corpus/
*.jsonl.gz
*.parquet
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal

# Build artefacts
/dist/
/coverage/
